page DocsProviderIps

title "IP addresses - Documentation"

template
<div class="min-h-[calc(100vh-4rem)] grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-[auto_1fr] bg-page transition-colors">

  <DocsSidebar active="provider-ips" />

  <div class="min-w-0 px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-10 py-6 sm:py-10">
  <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto">

    <article class="rounded-3xl border border-line bg-panel p-5 sm:p-8">
      <p class="text-zinc-500 text-[11px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] mb-3">Documentation / Cloud providers</p>
      <h1 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-light uppercase tracking-wide text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100">IP addresses</h1>
      <p class="text-zinc-500 text-sm mt-2 mb-8">Addresses in the account, their reverse DNS, and extra addresses you can allocate.</p>

      <h2 class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider mb-4">The list</h2>
      <p class="text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-3">Use the tabs to show <strong>All</strong>, <strong>IPv4</strong> or <strong>IPv6</strong>. Each row shows the address, the version, the region, what it is attached to and its reverse DNS. The type is Public, Private, Primary or Floating.</p>
      <h2 class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider mb-4">Allocate an address</h2>
      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-line overflow-hidden mb-8">
        <div class="px-5 py-3.5">
          <p class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 text-sm font-medium">Linode</p>
          <p class="text-zinc-500 text-xs mt-0.5">Adds an extra public IPv4 address to a Linode. Extra addresses are billed monthly.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="px-5 py-3.5 border-t border-stone-100 dark:border-white/5">
          <p class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 text-sm font-medium">Hetzner</p>
          <p class="text-zinc-500 text-xs mt-0.5">Creates a floating IP you can move between servers. Choose IPv4 or IPv6, then either <strong>For a server</strong> or <strong>In a location</strong> (its home location). Hetzner bills it monthly, assigned or not. A name is optional.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <h2 class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider mb-4">Reverse DNS</h2>
      <p class="text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-3">Reverse DNS maps an address back to a name. Mail servers check it, so set it for any server that sends email. Select <strong>Edit reverse DNS</strong>, type a name such as mail.example.com and save. Private addresses have none.</p>
      <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300 mb-8">
        <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 mt-2 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-brand-500"></span><span><strong>Linode</strong> only accepts a name that already has an A or AAAA record pointing at this address. Leave it empty to reset.</span></li>
        <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 mt-2 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-brand-500"></span><span><strong>Hetzner</strong>: leave it empty to reset. For IPv6 it sets the first address in the /64.</span></li>
      </ul>
      <h2 class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider mb-4">Release an address</h2>
      <p class="text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-3"><strong>Release</strong> gives the address back and stops the billing. It is only offered where the provider allows it:</p>
      <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300 mb-8">
        <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 mt-2 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-brand-500"></span><span>Linode: extra public IPv4 addresses. A server's primary address cannot be released.</span></li>
        <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 mt-2 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-brand-500"></span><span>Hetzner: floating IPs, and primary IPs that are not assigned. An assigned primary IP stays for as long as its server exists.</span></li>
      </ul>
      <h2 class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider mb-4">If something goes wrong</h2>
      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-line overflow-hidden mb-8">
        <div class="px-5 py-3.5">
          <p class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 text-sm font-medium">Couldn't allocate the address. Try again.</p>
          <p class="text-zinc-500 text-xs mt-0.5">Check the server or location you picked.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="px-5 py-3.5 border-t border-stone-100 dark:border-white/5">
          <p class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 text-sm font-medium">Couldn't save the reverse DNS. Try again.</p>
          <p class="text-zinc-500 text-xs mt-0.5">On Linode, add the A or AAAA record first, then save again.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="px-5 py-3.5 border-t border-stone-100 dark:border-white/5">
          <p class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 text-sm font-medium">Couldn't release that address.</p>
          <p class="text-zinc-500 text-xs mt-0.5">Read the message. The provider says why.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-3">If the API token is missing a permission this page needs, a message at the top says which one and how to fix it. Add the permission to the token at the provider, then reload.</p>

      <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-4 mt-8 pt-5 border-t border-stone-100 dark:border-white/5">
        <a href="/docs/providers/images" class="text-sm text-brand-600 dark:text-brand-500 hover:underline">&larr; Images</a>
        <a href="/docs/providers/domains" class="text-sm text-brand-600 dark:text-brand-500 hover:underline">Domains &rarr;</a>
      </div>
    </article>

  </div>
  </div>
</div>
